      "content": "To gauge neighborhood stability, consider incorporating metrics such as vacancy rates, crime indexes, and police response times. You can also explore external data sources like parcel data and voting records to capture community cohesion and socioeconomic factors. Weighting these factors inversely, with higher stability and cohesion correlating to lower risk, can help prioritize more robust borrowers. Additionally, consider using machine learning techniques like clustering or anomaly detection to identify outliers and robustness indicators in the data.",
