    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "those indicators make sense but we're worried about the data being too messy. if we're looking at things like \"cohesion,\" would it be more effective to look at specific neighborhood demographics or even the types of businesses that dominate an area? like, would a neighborhood with a high density of established, family-owned businesses vs. one with more transient/retail-heavy shops be worth different weightings in the risk profile?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
