      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Incorporating neighborhood demographics and business types can help capture unique community characteristics that contribute to stability. Weighting the risk model based on these factors, such as the density of family-owned businesses versus retail-heavy shops, can provide a more nuanced understanding of the local environment. You can even consider assigning weights to different business types based on their likelihood to contribute to long-term neighborhood stability, such as local services, manufacturing, or established businesses. This can help surface areas with stronger local ecosystems.",
